# harness/.operator-fix-surface
#
# Paths in the estree loop's fix surface that are maintained directly by the
# operator (human or coding agent) in the shared checkout, NEVER by the
# worker's model. main_loop_estree.pl's changed_since_snapshot consults this
# list: entries are never stashed by scoped_stash, regardless of whether they
# were dirty at the iteration snapshot.
#
# WHY (2026-10-21): the dirty-at-snapshot heuristic cannot see an edit made
# MID-iteration — it looks identical to the worker's own WIP — and it reverted
# the same operator addition (sh2.globMatch on the sh2 object) four times,
# each theft landing in a `estree-loop regression` stash.
#
# Format: one path per line, relative to the workspace root (or absolute).
# `#` comments and blank lines are ignored.

harness/sh2-namespace.mjs
harness/sh2-trace.mjs
harness/estree_gate.pl
# New transform file created by the operator's coding agent — no worker
# owns it, so ALL dirt in it is the operator's (untracked files cannot be
# stash-pathspecs anyway, but the list documents the ownership).
sh2perl/src/transforms/case_lowering.rs
# The rust renderer — operator surface for the rust-idiom work (the rust
# backend worktree keeps its own copies; the estree loop's model targets
# estree failures, not this file).
sh2perl/src/rust_backend.rs
